+On fixture identity switch or fixture logout, the UI aborts its pending requests and stops subsequent request steps. The browser test holds a message response after its database commit, switches actors and verifies no completion is dispatched and no old content appears for the new actor. Client abort cannot undo a server-committed message or cancel work already processed; the synthetic backend may leave the original owner's run pending with no automatic recovery. This does not establish server-side revocation or production cancellation semantics.
